"\\frac{11}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-252990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the fifth term of the sequence given by the recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=2{a}_{n-1}-3,\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-252990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Starting with the first term ${a}_{1}=5,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive formula until we reach the fifth term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =5 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2{a}_{1}-3=2\\cdot 5-3=7 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =2{a}_{2}-3=2\\cdot 7-3=11 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =2{a}_{3}-3=2\\cdot 11-3=19 \\\\ {a}_{5} & =2{a}_{4}-3=2\\cdot 19-3=35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fifth term is ${a}_{5}=35.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-252990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96257c6d488ad7c3eba54943b695f53bf3033d4da63a73d9ea0d3e69070a3096"} {"question" "q-252990" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-252990" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "19"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "32"] ["math" "35"] ["math" "41"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-252990" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "35"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the third term of the sequence given by the recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=3{a}_{n-1}-1,\\,{a}_{1}=-4,\\,n\\ge 2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Starting with the first term ${a}_{1}=-4,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive formula until we reach the third term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =-4 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =3{a}_{1}-1=3\\cdot (-4)-1=-13 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =3{a}_{2}-1=3\\cdot (-13)-1=-40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the third term is ${a}_{3}=-40.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96257c6d488ad7c3eba54943b695f53bf3033d4da63a73d9ea0d3e69070a3096"} {"question" "q-253349" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253349" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-121"] ["math" "-13"] ["math" "-26"] ["math" "-40"] ["math" "-74"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253349" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-40"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the fourth term of the sequence given by the recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=3{a}_{n-1}+2{a}_{n-2},\\,{a}_{1}=2,\\,{a}_{2}=4,\\,n\\ge 3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Starting with the initial terms ${a}_{1}=2,$ and ${a}_{2}=4,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive formula until we reach the fourth term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =2 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =4 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =3{a}_{2}+2{a}_{1}=3\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 2=12+4=16 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =3{a}_{3}+2{a}_{2}=3\\cdot 16+2\\cdot 4=48+8=56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fourth term is ${a}_{4}=56.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96257c6d488ad7c3eba54943b695f53bf3033d4da63a73d9ea0d3e69070a3096"} {"question" "q-253351" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253351" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "40"] ["math" "48"] ["math" "56"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253351" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "56"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the fourth term of the sequence given by the recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=2{a}_{n-1}-5,\\,{a}_{1}=6,\\,n\\ge 2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Starting with the first term ${a}_{1}=6,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive formula until we reach the fourth term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =6 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2{a}_{1}-5=2\\cdot 6-5=7 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =2{a}_{2}-5=2\\cdot 7-5=9 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =2{a}_{3}-5=2\\cdot 9-5=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fourth term is ${a}_{4}=13.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96257c6d488ad7c3eba54943b695f53bf3033d4da63a73d9ea0d3e69070a3096"} {"question" "q-253350" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253350" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "13"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253350" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "13"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following recurrence relations are first-order?\n\n- ${a}_{n}={a}_{n-1}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}$\n- ${b}_{n}=3{b}_{n-2}$\n- ${c}_{n}=\\frac{{c}_{n-1}}{3}-2{c}_{n-3}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The order of a recurrence relation is the largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding terms in the relation.\n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- The largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${a}_{n-1}$ in the relation is $1.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $1.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${b}_{n}$ and the preceding terms ${b}_{n-1}$ and ${b}_{n-2}$ in the relation is $2.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $2.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${c}_{n}$ and the preceding terms ${c}_{n-1}$ and ${c}_{n-3}$ in the relation is $3.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1cb9489dd3305aa49961946f721828978e386cfa2a891527ad0cf044ba4ed5"} {"question" "q-253468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96257c6d488ad7c3eba54943b695f53bf3033d4da63a73d9ea0d3e69070a3096"} {"question" "q-253468" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036387/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f1c